      ":question/problem": "Consider the initial value problem\n$y^{\u2032} = f(x, y), y(1) = 0$\nfor some function $f(x, y)$. The table below shows the intermediate quantities computed in the first iteration of the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method.\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | $y^{\u2032}$ | $y_{1}^{\u2032}$ | $y_{2}^{\u2032}$ | $y_{3}^{\u2032}$ | $\u0394y$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-1$ | $2$ |  |\n\nGiven that the step size is $\u0394x = 1$, at which of the following points is the function $f$ **NOT** evaluated during this iteration?"
