      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-331162",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose we wish to solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nand we take a step of size $\u0394x$ using the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method. Fill in the blanks to complete the weighted-average formula for the increment and the stage definitions, starting at the point $(x,y).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u0394y & =\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{\u2032}+2{y}_{1}^{\u2032}+2{y}_{2}^{\u2032}+{y}_{3}^{\u2032})\\cdot \u0394x \\\\ {y}^{\u2032} & =f(x,y) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{\u2032} & =f({{field-1}},\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{\u2032}\\cdot \u0394x) \\\\ {y}_{2}^{\u2032} & =f(x+\\frac{1}{2}\u0394x,\\,{{field-2}}) \\\\ {y}_{3}^{\u2032} & =f(x+\u0394x,\\,{{field-3}})\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    }
